{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211332-lunars","id":1211332,"title":"Lunars","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-04-25T02:27:56-07:00","id":1211332,"title":"Lunars","content":"I was just looking at the meeting notes and saw that Lunars is now in the first draft phase. What happened with Exigents, I thought that they were supposed to be next.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/706-rickayelm","name":"rickayelm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T03:05:36-07:00","id":1211340,"title":"","content":"Plans changed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T03:31:53-07:00","id":1211347,"title":"","content":"I was pretty mortified by it until the timetable for splat books started moving up.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T09:33:51-07:00","id":1211446,"title":"","content":"The new Devs decided it would be better to do Lunars first, and then Exigents. They announced it a while ago (4-6 months ago maybe? Not sure).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Currently, the announced timetable is:<br /> Dragonblood (the text is finished)<br /> The Realm<br /> Heirs of the Shogunate<br /> More Hundred Devils Night Parade (some will be out before the ones above, as it's released two entries at a time)<br /> More Antagonists of the Righteous (some will be out before the ones above, as it's released one-two entries at a time)<br /> Lunars<br /> ST Guide<br /> Exigents* (though Exigents hasn't officially been approved by the company yet, as it's too far in the future)<br /> <br /> *Which will also include an appendix with the fluff (and a quick guide to how to do them with the Exigents' rules) for the (non-canonical) Heart-Eaters, Umbral Exalted and Dream-Souled, who you can see in that spread in the Core with the Alchemical and Infernal. There's currently no plans to give those three splat books (unless one of them is really popular).<br /> <br /> I guess there will also be a smaller book or two between Lunars and Exigents. A location book maybe, something like that. But not a splat book.<br /> <br /> It's probably also worth pointing out that while the Devs do seem to intend to do Paths of Brigid at some point in the future, I haven't heard anything about Towers of the Mighty since the old devs left, so I suspect it's not happening (fine with me, other books look more interesting).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 04-25-2018, 05:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T09:42:20-07:00","id":1211449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211332-lunars?p=1211446#post1211446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's probably also worth pointing out that while the Devs do seem to intend to do Paths of Brigid at some point in the future, I haven't heard anything about Towers of the Mighty since the old devs left, so I suspect it's not happening (fine with me, other books look more interesting).</div> </div> </div> </div>Vance's noted that sorcery and Manses are both in need of books to cover them, albeit perhaps not in the same way as the previous dev team.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T09:58:28-07:00","id":1211452,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m not sure Heirs to the Shogunate will be out before Lunars, since they can\u2019t actually even start writing the outline until the Kickstarter finishes and they\u2019ve already started on Lunars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T10:00:40-07:00","id":1211453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/120518-star-wars-eu-more-exalted-than-star-wars?p=121144#post121144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, the Devs want to do a Storyteller's Guide at some point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty sure Vance has said that the ST guide is coming between Lunars and Exigents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5280-gfrobbin84","name":"gfrobbin84","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T10:25:09-07:00","id":1211459,"title":"","content":"About eight months ago, the devs mentioned that they decided they wanted to move Lunars before Exigents. This was done for two big reasons: to get another of the classical Exalted out into people's hands sooner (since for what we shall call only Reasons, the line is working from a trust deficit as concerns the release schedule) and to give the developers experience with having written another full Charm set (and an Attribute-based one as opposed to Ability) before writing an entire book on <i>how</i> to write Charm sets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Solar Kitten","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3907-aretii","name":"Aretii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3907_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T13:57:00-07:00","id":1211554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gfrobbin84</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211332-lunars?p=1211453#post1211453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pretty sure Vance has said that the ST guide is coming between Lunars and Exigents.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes; the pitch has been approved.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T14:53:25-07:00","id":1211574,"title":"","content":"For what it's worth, I <i>so strongly</i> support Lunars before Exigents. I'm also really looking forward to an ST guide, as I think that that could do a lot to make the line more accessible to players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/415-equitable-remedy","name":"Equitable Remedy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar415_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T17:50:28-07:00","id":1211618,"title":"","content":"Any word on sidereals? Do they get their own book in this edition or is that kind of a \u201cdown the road at some point thing\u201d along with liminals and abyssals presumably.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2116-jivex","name":"JiveX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2116_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T18:10:54-07:00","id":1211626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JiveX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211332-lunars?p=1211618#post1211618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any word on sidereals? Do they get their own book in this edition or is that kind of a \u201cdown the road at some point thing\u201d along with liminals and abyssals presumably.</div> </div> </div> </div>I personally hope it is after exigents, as sidereals are critical to the setting. Also I believe that in the past that some splats (Liminals and Getimain) were to be soft covers as they probably don't have the extensive history and society that other exalts require, so logically their books will be smaller. So we might see Getimain released along side sidereals. However things change and this may no longer be the case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2302-snakesandsuns","name":"Snakesandsuns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2302_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T18:22:44-07:00","id":1211633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Snakesandsuns</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211332-lunars?p=1211626#post1211626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally hope it is after exigents, as sidereals are critical to the setting. Also I believe that in the past that some splats (Liminals and Getimain) were to be soft covers as they probably don't have the extensive history and society that other exalts require, so logically their books will be smaller. So we might see Getimain released along side sidereals. However things change and this may no longer be the case.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, last I remember hearing Liminals would be a softcover released near to Abyssals and any other underworld/necromancy exploring stuff; and Getimians would theoretically be a softcover similarly alongside/released-soon-after Sidereals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 04-25-2018, 09:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T18:34:10-07:00","id":1211638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211332-lunars?p=1211633#post1211633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yeah, last I remembering hearing Liminals would be a softcover released near to Abyssals and any other underworld/necromancy exploring stuff; and Getimians would theoretically be a softcover similarly alongside/released-soon-after Sidereals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for confirming my thoughts. I really hope that the manse book comes up sooner rather than later. Sorcery can be held off a bit because new spells can come with each exalt.<br /> <br /> However on the note of Lunars, for a splat I don't particularly care about they sound to be a lot more interesting this go around! So I don't mind exigents getting displaced a bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2302-snakesandsuns","name":"Snakesandsuns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2302_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T00:11:14-07:00","id":1211708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JiveX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1211332-lunars?p=1211618#post1211618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any word on sidereals? Do they get their own book in this edition or is that kind of a \u201cdown the road at some point thing\u201d along with liminals and abyssals presumably.</div> </div> </div> </div>The classic Exalted (that's all the Exalted introduced in the previous editions - Solars, Dragon-Blooded, Lunars, Sidereals, Abyssals, Alchemicals, Infernals) all get hardbacks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":51,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","user":"marin","date":". 04-26-2018, 03:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}